# Solar Power System Simulator

A full-stack thesis-ready web application for the design, modeling, and evaluation of solar photovoltaic systems.

## Scope
This simulator includes:
- solar resource and irradiance input modeling
- PV array sizing and performance assumptions
- battery and inverter sizing considerations
- load profile analysis
- annual energy generation and load balance estimation
- performance ratio, capacity factor, specific yield, autonomy, and other engineering metrics
- economic evaluation (annual savings, LCOE, payback period, ROI-oriented indicators)
- environmental impact analysis (CO2 avoidance)
- a modern dashboard for visual explanation and scenario comparison

## Standards and assumptions
The simulator is designed for academic and design-stage analysis and is aligned with commonly used engineering references and standards including:
- IEC 61724 for PV performance monitoring and performance assessment
- IEC 60364 for electrical installation design principles
- NEC-aligned assumptions for general solar system planning and safety-oriented design logic

## Tech stack
- Frontend: React + TypeScript + Vite + Tailwind CSS + Recharts
- Backend: Node.js + Express + TypeScript
- API validation: zod

