## Start locally
```bash
npm install
npm run dev
```

Open the frontend at:
- http://localhost:5173

The backend API runs at:
- http://localhost:4000/api

## Example API request
```bash
curl -X POST http://localhost:4000/api/simulations/run \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "projectName": "Academic Microgrid",
    "location": {
      "latitude": 6.52,
      "longitude": 3.38,
      "altitudeM": 40,
      "ghiKwhM2Day": 5.4
    },
    "system": {
      "pvCapacityKw": 12,
      "panelEfficiency": 0.2,
      "panelAreaM2": 60,
      "tiltDeg": 15,
      "azimuthDeg": 180,
      "temperatureCoeffPerC": 0.004,
      "systemLossesPercent": 14,
      "inverterEfficiency": 0.96,
      "batteryCapacityKwh": 28,
      "maxDepthOfDischarge": 0.8,
      "batteryEfficiency": 0.92,
      "batteryPowerKw": 8
    },
    "load": {
      "dailyLoadKwh": 38,
      "peakLoadKw": 11,
      "loadProfile": [0.35, 0.3, 0.28, 0.32, 0.4, 0.7, 0.95, 1.1, 0.9, 0.7, 0.65, 0.52, 0.6, 0.8, 0.9, 1.0, 1.1, 1.2, 1.0, 0.75, 0.72, 0.66, 0.48, 0.38]
    },
    "economic": {
      "capitalCostUsd": 24500,
      "maintenanceCostUsdPerYear": 300,
      "energyPriceUsdPerKwh": 0.18,
      "discountRate": 0.08,
      "projectLifetimeYears": 20,
      "gridCarbonFactorKgPerKwh": 0.425
    }
  }'
```

## Notes
This project is intended for academic and design-oriented evaluation. Final engineering decisions should be validated with site-specific data, manufacturer datasheets, local regulatory codes, and professional engineering review.
